==== status
h2: High Availability Status
Real-time status of the HA cluster. Updates every 5 seconds.
h3: Cluster Status
| Cluster Overview
| Cluster State | DEGRADED
| Node Role | MASTER
| Instance: 1 | MASTER
| Instance: 2 | MASTER
| Last Synchronization
| Config Sync | <time>
| Lease Sync | <time>
h3: Service Status
| Service | Status | PID | Uptime
| keepalived | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
| owsync | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
| lease-sync | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
h3: Peer Status
| Peer Name | Address | State | Last Seen
| ha-node2 | 172.30.0.11 | Online | <time>
| edge-router | fd00:172:30::20 | Offline | Unreachable
| legacy | 172.30.0.12 | Offline | Unreachable
==== simple
h2: High Availability - General
Configure a high availability cluster with 2 or more routers. Advanced options are available in the Advanced pages.
h3: Cluster Configuration
config.enabled [CBI.FlagValue] Enable HA Cluster: [x]
  help: Enable high availability clustering on this router
config.node_priority [CBI.Value] Priority: value=150 (placeholder "100")
  help: VRRP priority (1-255). Higher priority becomes MASTER.
config.vrrp_transport [CBI.ListValue] VRRP Transport: select=unicast {multicast,unicast}
  help: Multicast is the default. Use unicast when multicast is unavailable on the network.
h3: Peer Routers
| Peer | 
| peer1: ha-node2 (172.30.0.11) | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| peer2: edge-router (fd00:172:30::20) | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| peer3: legacy (172.30.0.12) | [☰][Edit][Delete]
<button> Add
h3: Virtual IP Addresses
All VIPs share a single failover group and switch together. Use the Advanced page to create independent failover groups. Optional. If IPv6 is configured, keepalived creates a second instance with VRID+128.
| Interface | VRID | IPv4 Address | IPv6 Address | Enable | 
| lan: <img> lan | 51 (IPv6: 179) | 192.168.50.254 | fd00:192:168:50::254 | Yes | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| lan_old: <img> lan | 51 | 192.168.50.253 | none | No | [☰][Edit][Delete]
| vpn6: <img> backend | 52 (IPv6: 180) | none | fd00:172:30::254 | Yes | [☰][Edit][Delete]
<button> Add VIP...
h3: Configuration Synchronization
Select which /etc/config files to synchronize and how synchronization is performed.
config.encryption_key [CBI.Value] Encryption Key: password=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef (placeholder "Click "Generate New Key" button below to create a secure random key") button "∗"
  help: 256-bit AES encryption key (64 hexadecimal characters) for configuration sync (owsync) and DHCP lease sync (lease-sync). Must be identical on all cluster nodes. Leave empty to disable encryption.
config._generate_key [CBI.ButtonValue] Generate New Key: button "Generate New Key"
config._dhcp_leases [CBI.FlagValue] Enable Real-time DHCP Lease Sync: [x]
  help: Synchronize DHCP leases in real-time using the lease-sync daemon for seamless client failover
config.sync_method [CBI.ListValue] Sync Method: select=owsync {owsync,none}
  help: owsync: real-time file synchronization. none: disable file synchronization.
config._dhcp_config [CBI.FlagValue] Sync DHCP Configuration: [x]
  help: Synchronize /etc/config/dhcp (address pools, static leases, DNS settings)
config._firewall_config [CBI.FlagValue] Sync Firewall Rules: [x]
  help: Synchronize /etc/config/firewall (port forwarding, rules, zones). Review rules before enabling.
==== simple modal peer1
h4: High Availability - General
peer1.name [CBI.Value] Peer Name: value=ha-node2 (placeholder "router2")
peer1.address [CBI.Value] Peer IP Address: value=172.30.0.11 (placeholder "192.168.1.2")
peer1.source_address [CBI.ListValue] Source Address: select=172.30.0.10 {172.30.0.10,fd00:172:30::10,192.168.50.10,fd00:192:168:50::10}
  help: Local IP to use when contacting this peer. Must match address family (IPv4/IPv6) of peer.
peer1.sync_enabled [CBI.FlagValue] Enable Synchronization: [x]
  help: When disabled, this peer participates in VRRP failover but is excluded from config and lease sync. Use for non-OpenWrt peers.
<button> Dismiss
<button> Save
